------------------------------------------------------------------------------
PARITY SCOPE  (Honesty #2 No-scope-narrowing)
------------------------------------------------------------------------------
The web <StaggerContainer> is a PURE presentational MOTION WRAPPER. Its inputs are `children` + one
display-boundary hook (useMotionPreference()); it renders a motion.div whose `show` variant carries
`transition: { staggerChildren: reduce ? 0 : 0.06 }` — the cascade that delays each child's entrance. There
is NO fetch, NO React-Query cache, NO Promise -> therefore NO loading / error / stale / offline branch (there
is nothing to fetch, fail, age, or disconnect from; the hosted content owns its own data states).
Reproducing those generic states would FABRICATE behaviour the source does not have, so this surface
reproduces only the source's REAL branches — exactly the disposition the sibling presentational primitives
StaggerItem (0194), FadeIn (0191), RouteTransition (0192), and InlineCallout (0124) used. The REAL branches,
all reproduced + tested:
  • full-motion cascade : children enter hidden {opacity 0, y 15} -> shown {opacity 1, y 0} over 350 ms,
                          each delayed index * 0.06 s (web staggerChildren).
  • reduced-motion      : the cascade collapses to a no-op (staggerChildren=0); children render in their
                          final state {opacity 1, y 0}, no movement; childEntrance animation nil.
  • empty-content leaf  : the native never-a-blank-box peer of the container hosting no children.
  • stray child (inert) : a .staggerChild(index:) outside any container resolves to the .inert context
                          (phase already shown) and renders fully visible — the web peer of a <StaggerItem>
                          mounted without a <StaggerContainer> parent.
Data source  : useMotionPreference -> StaggerContainerMotionPreference.resolve (1:1 port; the live reduce
               flag binds via \.accessibilityReduceMotion, the native peer of useReducedMotion()).
Shared comps : none (the web source uses none).
Charts/maps  : none (the web source uses none) -> Swift Charts / MapKit not required.
i18n keys    : none in source (anonymous); only native a11y additions, resolved through the P1/S10 facade.
Telemetry    : view.opened emitted once with slug "StaggerContainer" (P1/S11).
a11y         : reduce-motion honored (the core behaviour, tested); Dynamic Type via tokens; the cascade
               wrapper is VoiceOver-transparent (adds no traits, leaving content semantics intact); the empty
               leaf is a single combined, labelled element. No interactive elements (vacuous for "label on
               every interactive element").

